## Frequently Asked Questions

{% faq
   title="Email FAQ"
   items=[
     {"question": "Why use React Email instead of plain HTML templates?", "answer": "React Email lets you write email templates using familiar JSX syntax with component reusability. It handles cross-client compatibility issues that make email HTML notoriously difficult. You get the same developer experience as your React components."},
     {"question": "How do I test emails without sending real ones?", "answer": "Use Mailpit in development (included in Docker setup). It captures all outgoing emails and shows them in a web UI at localhost:8025. For staging, use Resend's test mode or a dedicated test inbox service like Mailtrap."},
     {"question": "How do I avoid emails going to spam?", "answer": "Verify your sending domain in your email provider (SPF, DKIM, DMARC records). Use a consistent sender address. Keep HTML clean and avoid spam trigger words. Resend and Postmark have higher deliverability than self-hosted SMTP."},
     {"question": "Should I send emails synchronously in server actions?", "answer": "For critical emails (verification, password reset), yes - wait for confirmation. For notifications, consider queuing them with a service like Inngest or QStash to avoid blocking the user's action and enable retries."}
   ]
/%}

